@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam ranksep 55
skinparam nodesep 40

node "Navegador do usuário" as Browser {
  artifact "SPA React\n(TypeScript)" as SPA
}

node "Host (máquina local / servidor)" as Host {
  artifact "Frontend\nReact + Vite (build)" as Front
  node "Go runtime" as GoRT {
    component "authServer\n(:3001 — REST + WebSocket)" as Core
  }
  node "Node.js" as NodeRT {
    component "run-audit.mjs\n(Puppeteer)" as Runner
    component "Chromium\n(N instâncias)" as Chrome
  }
  database "MongoDB\n(:27017)" as Mongo
}

cloud "Internet" {
  component "Jitsi (meet.jit.si)" as Jitsi
  component "Whereby" as Whereby
  component "Zoom" as Zoom
}

SPA --> Front : HTTP (carrega a SPA)
SPA --> Core : HTTPS (REST) + WebSocket
Core --> Mongo : TCP 27017
Core --> Runner : spawn (processo Node)
Runner --> Chrome : controla
Chrome --> Jitsi : HTTPS/WSS (WebRTC)
Chrome --> Whereby : HTTPS/WSS (WebRTC)
Chrome --> Zoom : HTTPS/WSS (WebRTC)

note bottom of Host : Execução em host único (local). Em produção, os mesmos\nartefatos podem ser distribuídos: frontend estático hospedado,\nbackend Go + runner em servidor e MongoDB gerenciado.
@enduml
